  "behavior": [
    "List stores the actual BaseListStorage allocator/head/tail/extent. Individually allocated ListValueNode links are its authoritative traversal order; generic BaseList iterators point at those same nodes.",
    "Append, prepend, cursor insertion/removal, reverse and same-resource splices dispatch to raw base operations; exchange swaps the canonical base and its node owners.",
    "Mutable insert_list_before_at preserves native previous-link updates. Immutable wrappers retain existing Rust caller-state behavior.",
    "Cross-resource transfers copy one node at a time and retain native cursor-validation/copy-failure order; source destruction occurs only after successful copying.",
    "Node owners form an unordered Vec allocation registry. Shared linked-node release helper retains original allocator/layout and releases allocation even when user Drop unwinds; Sequence uses the same helper.",
    "Normal removal invokes Drop at the native callback point before count/tail/cursor completion. catch_unwind captures a destructor panic, allows raw metadata completion, then resumes the panic.",
    "Clear follows native destruction order. Unwinding resets canonical metadata and reclaims remaining owners rather than leaving safe access to freed nodes.",
    "Compile assertions retain List/iterators Send+Sync, List<PhantomPinned> Unpin and List unwind traits; Miri checks simultaneous mutable iterator items and panic paths."
  ],
